# Read by ripgrep, and by the search tools of hosts that are built on it, in whatever tree
# holds this skill folder. A project install puts the skill into the workspace
# (<workspace>/.claude/skills/sbom-recovery, <workspace>/.agents/skills/...), and a search
# of the repositories there would return lines from it. Measured with the skills then installed
# for two hosts, the portfolio as it then stood: a hidden-aware search for a C library function
# returned 44 files of the skills together against 1 of the product.
#
# This hides nothing from a person or from a model that opens a file by its path. It keeps
# the skill's own text, which carries the vocabulary of the task (component names, versions,
# licences, build-system words), out of searches of the code under analysis:
#   references/          the contract, the role file, the limits
#   scripts/             the tools, whose source holds the word lists of the analysis
#   assets/              the tables the analysis reads: library names, header maps, licence ids
# SKILL.md stays visible. The patterns are anchored to the skill folder, so a `scripts/` of a
# repository under analysis is still searched.
# To search the skill itself, ask for it: rg --no-ignore PATTERN <skill folder>.
/references/
/scripts/
/assets/
